> Hmmm, just had an intersting thought.  If and Alpha box is placed into a
> cluster with VMS boxed, this will be for queue sharing and data sharing.
> People are going to have to be very careful about accidentally executing code
> for a VAX on and Alpha box.  VMS is VMS from a user point of view, but the 
> executables are different for VMS and Alpha boxes, are they not?  This 
> obviously means a VAX boot disk and an Alpha boot disk
>  (heterogeneous cluster alert!!!) unless somebody in DEC is very
> clever about logicals and directory structures.  And ideas on the subject?
