While I'm not positive about this I'm pretty sure that the first release isn't
going to allow a shared queue system between the Alpha and VAX boxes.  I think
the main reason for this is that Alpha VMS is based mostly on one of the VMS
5.4 release levels with a smattering of features from later releases of VMS
including some future major release of VMS (aka v6.0) and so they haven't put
the new queue manager on it yet.

In any event, your comments about the incompatability of images are correct. 
You will need to have different boot disks for the VAX and Alpha boxes, but you
can still share UAF, Rightslist, and the other major databases not to mention
the disk farm.  You'll also need to have Alpha compatable images for any
applications you wish to run on the Alpha platform with their own set of
logicals to point to the correct directories.

