instr-sched.c has been added to the DEC/Alpha archives on
gatekeeper.dec.com and crl.dec.com. (gatekeeper is on the West
Coast and crl in on the East coast.)  Look in ~ftp/pub/DEC/Alpha.

instr-sched.c is a basic block instruction scheduler for the
Digital Alpha  21064-AA microprocessor.

It's purpose is to rewrite a basic block of alpha instructions
in such a way as to minimize stalls and maximize the number
of multiple issue slots kept full.

This scheduler would be useful, for example, in a compiler
back-end or optimizer.

A main program is attached which illustrates the operation of
the scheduling subroutine.

