First off, heat and power.  The NVAX chip isn't your run-of-the-mill 
two watt chip and takes a considerable amount of air movement and power
in order to run the chip.  That said, the packaging of the Model 60 and 90
wouldn't suffice, and thus we'd have to build yet another box.  It may
come as a surprise, but building boxes isn't cheap, and we've got to "pick
our battles" so to speak.  

There's also some considerable cost and performance implications in an MP
system.  (for instance you can tune the memory system when you don't have
to worry about snoopy caches, and bus arbitration)  

Believe me, we've thought about MP workstations, we've actually done 
them in the past (BTW, the 3520/3540 were considerably more expensive than
the Model 60, which has the same single stream performance as a 3540 has 
multi-stream)
