                 REGISTRATION MATERIALS FOR DECUS FALL 1992 
                SEMINARS AND SYMPOSIUM PROGRAMS NOW AVAILABLE


Registration materials for the DECUS Fall 1992 Seminars and Symposium - 
scheduled for December 5-11, 1992, at the Las Vegas Convention Center, Las 
Vegas, Nevada - are now available. In excess of 70,00 registration brochures 
are currently being mailed to DECUS U.S. Chapter members and other computing 
professionals across the country.

The semiannual national events, sponsored by the U.S. Chapter of the Digital 
Equipment Computer Users Society, are considered by many to be the most 
comprehensive forums on computing in the Digital computing arena. 

By attending the DECUS Fall 1992 Seminars and Symposium programs you will be 
exposed to a breadth of training and professional networking opportunities 
you can't get at any other single event. The cost and time effective format 
of the programs allow you to target in on the information you and your 
organization need to be more successful.

Computing professionals requiring in-depth training on specific technical 
topics can choose from 119 one- and two-day seminars. These quality seminars 
are filled on a first-come first-served basis. The symposium program consists 
of over 1200 hours of sessions, providing something for every computing 
professional. 

COPIES OF THESES DOCUMENTS ARE NOW AVAILABLE:

* DECUS Fall 1992 Seminars/Symposium Registration Brochure complete with 
Early-Bird Registration and Hotel Reservations forms - Register and secure 
your hotel requirements by November 4, 1992 and realize a substantial 
savings. 

* Seminar Abstracts - Outlines of materials covered during the one- and 
two-day seminars including speaker credentials and attendees prerequisites.

* Sessions-At-A-Glance (SAGs) - A listing of all symposium sessions presented 
on a given day. SAGs identify the title, scheduled location and time of 
sessions.

* Symposium Index - A listing of all symposium sessions scheduled to be 
presented, listed by stream of interest.

* Fall 1992 Seminars Symposium Registration Program - A complete program of 
all seminars/symposium activities.

* DECUS Library and SIG Tape Submissions - Share your software programs with 
others by submitting them to the DECUS Library. Simply bring an extra 
hardcopy directory listing and a hardcopy of the program abstract along with 
your DECUS Library submission to the Library Booth at symposium.

The DECUS Special Interest Group (SIG) tape program also accepts software 
submissions to use in the creation of DECUS SIG tapes. The contents of these 
tapes focus on specific streams of interest as established by the DECUS 
Special Interest Groups. 

* The Fall 1992 Symposium DECUS Library Offerings - Find out more information 
about the latest and some of the more popular DECUS Library offerings which 
are available for purchase via the Fall 1992 Seminars/Symposium Early-Bird 
Registration Invoice Form.

* DECUS Spring 1993 Symposium Call For Participation Kit - DECUS Invites you 
to submit sessions for the Spring 1993 Symposium program to be held June 
5-11, in Atlanta, Georgia. Submissions can take on a variety of formats, such 
as a formal paper, a panel discussion, or a question and answer session. Call 
today for your Call For Participation kit which includes more information, a 
submission form, abstract guidelines, and commercialism policy. 

* DECUS Membership Application - If you cannot attend the Fall 1992 Seminars 
and Symposium programs but would like to join DECUS, call for your membership 
application today. DECUS membership is free, and is granted on an individual 
basis to anyone with a bona fide interest in Digital computing.

DECUS members have access to year-round training programs, published 
materials, and a wide selection of public domain software.

HERE'S HOW TO GET MORE INFORMATION:

Copies of the:

* DECUS Fall 1992 Seminars/Symposium Registration Brochure - complete with 
copies of the Early-Bird Registration and Hotel Reservation forms. 
* Seminars Abstracts
* Sessions-At-A-Glance (SAGs)
* Symposium Index
* DECUS Library and SIG Tape Submission Forms and Library Offerings     
descriptions
* DECUS Spring 1993 Symposium Call For Participation Kit
* DECUS Membership Application

Can be obtained by simply calling 1-800-358-2614

A complete file containing all Seminar Abstracts and the Symposium Sessions 
Index may be viewed on-line via:

Digital's Electronic Connection - Those unfamiliar with the Electronic 
Connection may view the Seminar Abstracts and Symposium Sessions Index, as 
well as other DECUS information after registering for a free on-line account. 
Just dial 1-800-234-1998 at 1200 through 9600 baud from 7 A.M. to midnight, 
Eastern Time, with any Digital compatible terminal or PC, and enter #2 on the 
Welcome Screen. 

From the Main Menu enter the following series of numbers: #6 News From 
Digital; #3 DECUS Menu; and look for the National Seminars Abstracts and 
Symposium Sessions Index entries under #2 DECUS Seminars, Conferences and 
Symposia.

For additional assistance in accessing the Electronic Connection call 
1-800-DIGITAL.

DECUServe - Those with access to Internet TELNET can connect to 
decuserve.decus.org or connect via modem by calling 508-842-0200 DF 196 modem 
1200/2400/9600/CPS. Log in under Username: DECUSPROGRAM and follow the 
instructions on the bottom of each menu.

This file provides a keyword search option allowing you to produce a 
customized roadmap of your participation at the seminars and symposium 
programs.

Credit card registrations and registration questions should be directed to 
the DECUS Seminars/Symposium Registration line at: 508-841-3341.

If you have received a Fall 1992 Seminars/Symposium Early-Bird Registration 
Invoice Form, you can register with your credit card via FAX at: 
508-841-3373. 

Information on other DECUS products and services can be obtained by 
contacting DECUS Customer Service at: 508-841-391.


