finds a market is because of the usability issues you point out about
VAXnotes.  The gist of the problem you are describing is that VAXnotes was
designed for DEC's internal use BY engineers FOR engineers, and its
conferencing paradigm was not simplified for non-engineering users.

I will compare and contrast Huddle with VAXnotes for your benefit and that of
other INFO-VAX readers.  I am a technical sales and support person at
Innovative Software, but I will try to be as objective as possible.

