For our standards user login, GID==UID, so that everyone starts out
with a private environment.  As soon as we started running the DEC
named slaves serving hesiod, we found that the named processes would
blow up in size (not on the servers, as you note).  The problem is
that the GIDs are not all in the group database.  The slave must lose
track of the GIDs it is caching if the lookup fails in group.  I guess
we could fix it by installing GID entries in group for the 3,600 login
IDs.

Of course, if there are other memory leaks, then this one may not
match yours, either.


