Have you ever seen the internal cabling for the 5000/125?  The internal disk
cable on the 3min is shipped terminated.

> > 
> > If I connect an external disk or tape, it then reports that it has six RZ25's
> > connected and nothing else.
> 
> That sounds like one of your external devices has the same SCSI ID as the
> RZ25

Now this points to precisely what is the problem.  The documentation for the
RZ25's is just plain wrong.  To set the SCSI unit id you have to take the
bracket off it and on one side you'll see three jumpers which have set the
drive up to be unit 7.  When one reports it's unit 7 you get N of them and
no other device on the bus gets seen.  Fix up the unit id, put the bracket on
and boot it up.


