(Personal Opinion)

Within Digital, the VAXnotes conferences are widely used by a great 
crossection of the community. This includes PHD SW and HW engineers,
financial analysts, clerks, technicians, secretaries, managers etc.

Subjects covered are literally soup to nuts (ref the cookery and automotive
conferences....)

What I am trying to point out is that people from _very_ diverse backgrounds
and levels of expertise and training find the tool usable.

NOTES satisfies, in my belief all of your "Must Have"s

It also satisfies the "Like To have"s with qualification:
	-menu driven: Keypad and/or command driven for VTxxx terminals.
		Anyone familiar with keypad driven editors such as EDT and 
		suchlike will have no trouble at all.
		-DX/DECwindows/Motif interface for those with the right 
		 equipment.
	-search by author, date range, subject or keywords
	-Spell checker trivially included with your editor choice
	 customization, but noy=t imbedded in Notes.
	-Access through membership. Moderators assign membership, and also
	 restrict/set_unseen etc as required
      In other words, I believe the wish items to be well satisfied by NOTES.

As for  "BELLS AND WHISTLES", I am not sure what you mean exactly by 
variable output format/extent. Your header identifier is customizable.
Supports, (I believe , but check this) sixel/regis. Definitely supports
DDIF graphics, - this under the DECwindows/Motif interface.



BTW you may also like to look at VAX VTX as a few-to-many means of 
information dissimination if you have such a need.


opinions are mine but may be biased...

Mike


